## Reflection

This challenging project introduced binary decoding and showed how a small number of input bits can uniquely select one of several outputs.

Completing this project marked the end of my introduction to combinational logic in Verilog.

## Problems

No major problems occured during this project.

The main challenge was understanding the purpose of a decoder compared to a demultiplexer. While both activate outputs based on a control signal, the decoder generates unique output patterns directly from binary inputs rather than routing a data signal.

